  "description": "Routine maintenance dressing applied to aged leather bindings to keep the covering supple and slow deterioration. A light, non-staining, non-tacky preservative is worked sparingly into the surface with a soft cloth, concentrating on the spine and hinge areas where flexing is greatest. Cockerell argues that frequent handling and a thin oily film prolong leather life far better than hard coatings, which crack at the joint.",
